# --- Go build outputs (bead pg2-aq3cy) --------------------------------------
#
# WHY THIS IS NOT COSMETIC. A stray build output leaves the canonical clone
# DIRTY, and the ff-merge landing handler halts unless `git status --porcelain`
# there is empty -- so a single hand-run `go build` blocks ALL landing into this
# repo until the artifact is removed.
#
# THE LAYOUT RULE, not a list of paths. `go build` with no `-o` writes the
# executable into the CURRENT directory, named after the last element of the
# main package's import path -- which in every layout here equals the main
# package's own directory name. Re-derive the package set with
# `fd -t f main.go packages/`; it has exactly two shapes, so a build lands in
# exactly two positions:
#
#   packages/<pkg>/cmd/<bin>/<bin>   built from inside the main-package dir
#                                    (7 of 8 packages use this nested layout)
#   packages/<pkg>/<bin>             built from the module root -- either
#                                    `go build ./cmd/<bin>`, or a FLAT main
#                                    package such as pa-monitor-decorator-scope
#                                    (its module holds a single main package,
#                                    so even `go build ./...` emits a binary;
#                                    every other module has several packages,
#                                    for which `./...` discards the results)
#
# Git has no "only if executable" predicate and no backreference for "basename
# equals parent directory name", so the rules below ignore EVERY entry at those
# two positions and then re-include (a) every subdirectory and (b) every name
# carrying a file extension. Verified 2026-08-17: no tracked file sits
# extensionless at either position -- `git ls-files packages/ | rg '/[^/.]+$'`
# matches only `completions/` and `testdata/` entries, which are deeper and so
# unaffected.
#
# DO NOT reintroduce a case-class anchor such as `/packages/*/[a-z]*` to spare
# capitalised names. `core.ignorecase` is true on macOS (APFS), so `[a-z]` there
# matches `Makefile` and `LICENSE` too -- it would ignore them on darwin and
# keep them on NixOS, i.e. platform-divergent ignore behaviour in a repo that
# targets both. The explicit `!` allowlist below is deterministic instead.
#
# POLICY (RFC 2119):
#  - A newly added Go package MUST NOT require a new line here. Appending a
#    literal binary path is the defect this block replaces; it superseded the
#    single `/packages/pa-monitor/pa-monitor` line, which covered one package
#    and only the module-root position.
#  - A tracked file placed DIRECTLY at either position MUST carry a file
#    extension, or MUST be added to the conventional-name allowlist below.
#    Otherwise it is ignored silently and `git add -A` will skip it.
#  - Tooling that builds Go code SHOULD pass `go build -o <tmpdir>/...` so
#    nothing is produced in the source tree at all. Every in-repo call site
#    already does: `claude-extended-tool-approver/scripts/probe-*.sh`,
#    `packages/pb/internal/gate/lifecycle_smoke_test.go`, pa-monitor's
#    reexec/rpcclient tests, and all nix gomod2nix builds. These rules exist
#    for the bare hand-run `go build`, which no script can intercept.
/packages/*/*
!/packages/*/*/
!/packages/*/*.*
/packages/*/cmd/*/*
!/packages/*/cmd/*/*/
!/packages/*/cmd/*/*.*

# Conventional extensionless files that are NOT build output. Bracket classes
# spell both cases so the result is identical on case-sensitive filesystems.
!/packages/*/[Mm]akefile
!/packages/*/[Jj]ustfile
!/packages/*/Dockerfile
!/packages/*/LICENSE
!/packages/*/COPYING
!/packages/*/CODEOWNERS
!/packages/*/cmd/*/[Mm]akefile

# `go test -c` output. Placed after the re-includes above, which would
# otherwise put it back (it carries an extension). Generalises the same line in
# packages/ccpool/.gitignore, which stays for its `*.db` / `*.out` entries.
*.test

# Beads / Dolt files (added by bd init)
.dolt/
*.db
.beads-credential-key

# beads: local-only (data lives in dolt; nothing under .beads/ is tracked)
.beads/

# Claude Code per-session worktrees (runtime state, created by EnterWorktree)
.claude/worktrees/

# sp-bd-bridge per-session cache (local-only)
.perles/

# pre-commit-config.yaml is a symlink into /nix/store regenerated by the
# devShell's pre-commit hook setup. Different store paths on different
# machines.
.pre-commit-config.yaml
